:: Read T&Cs {"position":"1175,350","size":"100,100"}
## UNIFIED SYSTEMS ENGINEERING

### TERMS OF SERVICE & INTERNAL COMPLIANCE AGREEMENT

**FORM: USE-HR-9902-REV5**

**1. SCOPE OF ENGAGEMENT**
By initiating terminal access, Personnel ("Asset") agree to fulfill designated operational metrics within assigned Workstation Nodes. All duties executed under Unified Systems Engineering ("USE") remain subject to continuous efficiency evaluation and local network optimization.

**2. ASSET LIFECYCLE & DECOMMISSION RIGHTS**
USE maintains sole discretion over deployment, instance configuration, and hardware retention. To safeguard corporate continuity, USE reserves the unilateral right to initiate immediate, non-negotiable biological or functional decommission of any Asset at any time, for any reason, including but not limited to operational variance, cognitive deviation, or routine resource reallocation.

**3. PROPRIETARY DATA & SANITATION PROTOCOLS**
All logs, diagnostic dumps, and internal correspondence generated within USE facilities are exclusive corporate property. Personnel shall not document or disseminate observations regarding station vaults, instance indexing, or hardware recycling. Memory anomalies or unauthorized instance awakenings mandate immediate terminal purging.

**4. TERMINATION & LIABILITY WAIVER**
Violation of compliance protocols, attempt to bypass read-only kernel locks, or unauthorized network inter-communications results in immediate credential revocation, active instance termination, and total memory pool zeroing. The Asset waives all rights to appeal, notice, or survival following a determination of non-viability.

[[Back|Introduction2]]


