:: office4 {"position":"2425,850","size":"100,100"}
Person: "Office worker in the files and archives dept hu?
Wow. That must be pretty boaring. Though today was your first day by the look of things.
Why are you even down here? This is the old office from when USE ran a newspaper."
$playerName: "I might of triggered the emergency overide allarm."
Person: "How on your first day did u do that?"
$playerName: "Someone was rather lazy and left a box that said overide in the drawer. So once i unlocked it i might of set an alarm off. I didnt want to get fired so I went down the trapdoor that opened.
Person: "Well $playername, i suppose now you've given away your story of how you got here, i suppose I must give mine."

[[Continue|office5]]


:: office5 {"position":"2250,725","size":"100,100"}
Person: "My name is Robert Garrison."
(after: 2s)[(goto: "office6")]


:: office6 {"position":"2150,725","size":"100,100"}
Robert: "I was hired by United Systems Engineering under the guise of an IT technology consultancy. I had no idea why when I got interviewed. Why would a mainstream tech firm want someone with a high-level background in neurological science? Then I found out why. 
USE deals in cloning."

$playerName: "You. Are. Mad."

Robert: "No, I'm not. Once they realized I had an engineering degree, they reassigned me to maintenance—specifically to keep the neural transfer tanks running. But when the whole operation started falling apart, they tried to dispose of us. Over ten employees including my brother from different departments were targeted to cover their tracks."

$playerName: "No. It can't be."

Robert: "Yes, it can. Think about it. You read those terms and conditions: 'USE reserves the unilateral right to initiate immediate, non-negotiable biological or functional decommission of any Asset at any time, for any reason.'
Just think about it. The introduction booklet as well: 'Our facility specializes in mass-scale replication.' The evidence was hiding in plain sight the entire time."

Robert: "You agreed to the fact that they can kill you: 'including but not limited to operational variance, cognitive deviation, or routine resource reallocation.'
You didn't realize the consequences of accepting these terms. None of us did—and we paid for it dearly."

Robert: "The three of us who survived have tried to escape, but the most we could do was evade security officers. So this is where we've been living."

Robert: "We have been trying to uncover files but have been quite usuccsessful as we have no ID cards."

[[Continue|office7]]


:: office7 {"position":"1975,625","size":"100,100"}
